# The provider lock file IS committed (infra/terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl): it
# pins provider versions so a later apply cannot silently pick up a new one.

# Credential files. Never committed, under any name.
#
# An AWS key CSV was found in the working directory of this repo. It was never
# tracked, but `git add -A` would have taken it, and a pushed access key is
# compromised from the moment it is pushed -- rotation is the only remedy, not
# deletion, because the history keeps it.
*credentials*.csv
*credentials*.json
*accessKeys*.csv
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
